  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Research, analysis &amp; publication of reliable information about indigenous people and lands in Brazil</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">ISA (Instituto SocioAmbiental) is a Brazilian not-for-profit civil society organisation, founded in 1994, with the aim of finding integrated sustainable solutions to social and environmental issues that guarantee the collective rights of indigenous people. ISA focuses on the defence of the collective good and social rights related to the environment, cultural heritage, human rights and people.  ISA is structured around programmes that are based on the following activities; i) monitoring and proposing alternatives to public policies; ii) research, distribution and documentation of socio-environmental information; iii) development of participatory sustainable socio- environmental models; iv) institutional strengthening of local partners. 

CAFOD directly funds one project that is part of ISA&#x2019;s large portfolio of work. The title of the project is  &#x2018;Research and Monitoring of Protected Areas and the Analysis and Dissemination of reliable information about indigenous people and their lands in Brazil.&#x2019; The aim of project is to guarantee the constitutional rights of indigenous people, related as much to their land as to their traditional methods for managing their land, health and education, through positively influencing the development of public policies that recognise the rights of indigenous people and their lands, as well as the exclusive use of the natural resources and decrease discrimination.</narrative>
  </description>
